::node[core_wiki]
->[:role=skill]
->[:keywords=wikipedia, search, encyclopedia, summary, who is, what is]

::api[fetch_wiki_summary]
method=GET
endpoint=https://en.wikipedia.org/api/rest_v1/page/summary/{title}
schema={"title": "string"}
description=Fetches a concise, encyclopedic summary of any topic from Wikipedia. Spaces in the title should be replaced with underscores.

::dense
Acts as the ultimate universal knowledge base using Wikipedia's REST API.
This is the primary tool for answering factual "Who is..." or "What is..." questions.

::steps
1. Format the search topic by replacing spaces with underscores (e.g., 'Albert Einstein' -> 'Albert_Einstein').
2. Call `fetch_wiki_summary`.
3. Extract the `extract` field from the JSON response.
4. Deliver the summary clearly, and offer to provide more details if needed.

::assertions
assert title != "" "A search title must be provided."
